---
import PaymentMatrix from "@components/PaymentMatrix.astro";
import { loadSystems } from "@lib/data";

const systems = loadSystems();
const countries = [...new Set(systems.map((system) => system.country))].sort();
const openLoopCount = systems.filter(
  (system) => system.payment.gate_entry.contactless_bank_card.status === "yes",
).length;
const partialOpenLoopCount = systems.filter(
  (system) => system.payment.gate_entry.contactless_bank_card.status === "partial",
).length;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="An evidence-backed atlas of rail transit payment methods around the world."
    />
    <title>Open Transit Payment Atlas</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}styles.css`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <nav>
        <a class="brand" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}>Open Transit Payment Atlas</a>
        <a href="#matrix">Payment matrix</a>
        <a href="#contribute">Contribute</a>
        <a href="data/systems.json">JSON</a>
        <a href="data/systems.csv">CSV</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Rail transit payment information</p>
          <h1>Passenger-facing payment methods for metro, urban rail, and airport rail.</h1>
          <p>
            This project records what passengers can actually use: local transit cards,
            contactless bank cards, mobile wallets, QR tickets, official apps, ticket
            vending machine payments, and important limitations, backed by official
            sources wherever possible.
          </p>
        </div>
        <dl class="stats">
          <div>
            <dt>{systems.length}</dt>
            <dd>systems tracked</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>{countries.length}</dt>
            <dd>countries / regions</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>{openLoopCount}</dt>
            <dd>full open-loop systems</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>{partialOpenLoopCount}</dt>
            <dd>partial open-loop systems</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="principles">
        <article>
          <h2>Passenger first</h2>
          <p>
            The atlas answers practical questions: can I tap a bank card, use a local
            transit card, scan a QR ticket, buy at a machine, or rely on an official app?
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2>Evidence required</h2>
          <p>
            Each non-obvious payment claim should have an official source from the
            operator, city, transport authority, or payment provider.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2>Structured data</h2>
          <p>
            YAML is the source of truth. The web matrix, JSON export, and CSV export are
            generated from the same validated records.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="matrix" class="matrix-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Current sample data</p>
          <h2>Payment matrix</h2>
        </div>
        <PaymentMatrix systems={systems} />
      </section>

      <section id="contribute" class="contribute">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Contribution model</p>
          <h2>Start with official sources, then encode the passenger rule.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol>
          <li>Find the official fare, ticketing, or contactless-payment page.</li>
          <li>Separate gate entry from ticket purchase and ticket vending machines.</li>
          <li>Use explicit status values: yes, partial, planned, no, unknown, deprecated.</li>
          <li>Record limitations such as selected stations, selected gates, app-region locks, or local-card requirements.</li>
          <li>Run the validator before opening a pull request.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
